{{DIAGRAM:M4.S32.T32.C178.IMG1}}
$1$. Draw a polygon with the angles $A$, $B$, $C$ acute, $E$ right, $D$ and $F$ obtuse
Answer: A six-sided figure (hexagon ABCDEF) works: $\angle A$, $\angle B$ and $\angle C$ are acute, $\angle E$ is a right angle, $\angle D$ and $\angle F$ are obtuse (as shown in the solutions drawing).

